WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.650
News! I've got big news!

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.020
What's up, Yasu?

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.280
Actually...

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.780
Gyanko from St. Odessa lost the practice match?

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.660
No way!

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.030
It's for real.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.530
And their opponents were a middle-school team.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:19.910
Which school?

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.370
The private Seiho Academy.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.710
Seiho?

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.420
That team never makes it past the first round.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.840
So Gyanko of Odessa has fallen to Earth.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.090
You can't really say that.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.470
Kousaka Yuuma is on Seiho's team.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:37.890
Kousaka?

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.930
Didn't he win the Grand Prix in this year's Artistic Gunpla Contest?

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.020
There's also a fighter who uses some weird martial art.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.700
Japan's top middle-school builder, and a mysterious martial artist...

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.870
We'll win anyway.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.920
Under water, we are invincible.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.930
Why is that guy on the jungle gym?

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.340
Don't look at him!

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:25.060
No matter who opposes me, I won't lose.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.980
Isn't that right, Mamoru?

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.500
Sekai, Yuu, and I formed team Try Fighters.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.920
We successfully entered the Gunpla Battle Championship.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:21.300
And now we're practicing hard for the West Tokyo qualifiers which will be held in one month.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.010
Come on, Sekai!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.980
Jigen Haoh style!

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.730
<i>Shippu-Zuki: Gale Thrust!</i>

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.730
Shippu-Zuki!

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.030
He overpowered Mr Ral's Gouf!?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.620
He let him do it.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.080
What do you think, Mr Ral?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.370
So this is Sekai's Jigen Haoh style.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.630
Right. You have good fists.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.960
But... how about this?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.090
<i>Field changed to 1, Space.</i>

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.970
We're now in space?

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.310
Try your technique on me again.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.140
As you wish!

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.390
Jigen Haoh style!

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:16.900
I can't hold my stance.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.150
I see. There's no ground.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.360
Then, Senpu Tatsumaki-Geri!

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.360
<b><i>Senpu Tatsumaki-Geri: Whirlwind Spinning Kick</i></b>

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.790
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.220
My... Jigen Haoh style...

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.260
Sekai.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:52.310
You're controlling Gunpla based on the kenpo skills you've acquired in person.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.020
But its true power can only be effective

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.810
under the gravity you've physically experienced.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.400
Gunpla Battle's fields include outer space,

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.860
the lunar surface with 1/6 gravity,

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.780
and under water with high pressure.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.500
Unless you can use the   Jigen Haoh style in any situation,

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.210
you won't be able to win the Championships.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:16.960
Yes, sir.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.880
Good thing the battle damage was set to minimum level.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.680
Otherwise, your Gunpla would've been pulverized.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.600
Yuu, where're you going?

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.810
I'll go back home and work.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.390
I have more equipment at home.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:38.850
I'll be looking forward to it.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.360
Seeing the performance of the upgraded Lightning Gundam.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.910
Shall we practice again?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:51.870
Mr Ral.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.910
Before that, can I talk to you?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.120
What is it?

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:02.250
I want to change the Gunpla I'm using in the championships.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:09.640
I thought hard after our practice match with Gyanko.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:15.980
Sekai's Build Burning Gundam is a super-close attack type.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.020
Yuu's Lightning Gundam is a long-range shooting type.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:26.860
To make the most of them, I thought my machine should be a medium-range type,

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.700
which can also fight as an all-round support type.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.950
I see. That's a good point, but...

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:40.170
Then isn't your Powered GM Cardigan enough?

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.290
I want to improve its firepower and mobility.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:47.590
How about the Blue Destiny, which has an EXAM system?

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.840
I don't think it's a supporty type.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.510
How about the Gundam Ground Type?

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.180
It can carry support weapons in the container on its back.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.520
Then its mobility would decrease,

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.270
and the Ground Type can't handle every kind of terrain.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:06.730
Firepower, mobility, and weapons payload as well...

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.900
I thought about using a mobile armor,

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:13.620
but three people have to control it in the championship.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:18.580
Then let's use the Gouf, Fumina!

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.170
Mr. Ral, were you listening to what I said?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.000
It was a joke, a joke!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:28.630
Hey, I'm serious.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.300
Sorry, sorry.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:33.550
I have no clue what they're talking about.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:40.060
When you build a new machine, you don't have to choose from the Gunpla in the club room.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:45.560
Tomorrow is Sunday. Why don't you go to G-Muse?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.400
Yes. I was thinking of that, too.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:51.780
Hoshino, what's G-Muse?

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.700
G-Muse is...

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:57.370
Why not go with her, Sekai?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.660
Of course, you need to train,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:05.250
<i>but it's also important you learn what Gundam and Gunpla are all about.</i>

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:07.340
R-Right.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.170
Sekai, do you have time tomorrow?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.800
Yeah, I do...

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:13.930
Then let's go on a date.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:15.760
Kidding.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:16.930
Okay...

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.810
It's been a while since my bottom feels itchy once again.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:26.940
Hey, big sister?

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.400
Yeah?

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.690
What should I wear on a date?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.120
Are you going on a date?

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:36.740
Yes.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:37.830
With who?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:38.830
With Hoshino.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.160
With Miss Hoshino?

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:40.750
Yeah.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:44.620
Is that right...  with Miss Hoshino.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.290
How did you ask her out?

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.550
She was the one who asked me out.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:51.510
I-I see...

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.840
She's bolder than I had imagined.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.300
So what should I wear?

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:57.510
Well...

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.100
You should wear what you normally wear.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.930
There's no point making yourself uncomfortable with something you're not used to.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.600
So it's that simple.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.230
I guess.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.820
By the way, what's a date?

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.440
You need me to tell you that!?

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.630
Sekai!

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:36.050
You're early! It's still 10 minutes before we're supposed to meet.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:39.010
My sister told me never to be late.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.640
She also said to act and dress normally.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:42.970
I see.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.390
Then it's a bit early, but let's go.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.020
Yeah.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.060
You look different when you're out of uniform.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.070
I guess dressing normally feels unexpectedly awkward instead.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:55.610
Father, mother. Sekai can be a little weird,

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:58.910
but he's growing up into a healthy boy.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:05.080
To prevent the rash mistakes made by adolescent boys,

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.250
I'll watch him very closely.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.090
What?

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.930
An ill omen...

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.070
We're almost there.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:34.230
Yeah.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.160
Sekai, close your eyes for a sec.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:43.780
Why?

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.240
Just do it.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.080
Okay.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.920
This way.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:56.760
Miss Hoshino... How bold she is!

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.050
Keep your eyes closed.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.730
Sekai. you're rushing up the stairs of adulthood.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.480
Your sister thinks it's too early for you for that!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.900
Sekai, Open your eyes.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.900
No!!

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.630
A-Awesome...

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.800
What a huge Gunpla!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:43.760
Right?

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.640
It's actually not a Gunpla, but a life-size Gundam statue.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.930
There are so many people here.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.770
Gunpla is really popular, huh?

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:55.730
Well... It's more like Gundam instead of Gunpla that's popular...

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.980
Awesome.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.110
Gunpla is so awesome!

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:02.450
The inside's also fun. Let's go!

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:03.030
Yeah.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.620
Yup, your sister trusts you both.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:13.620
But still... This Gunpla is really awesome.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:31.850
Are these all Gunpla!?

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.520
How many of them are there?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.780
Hoshino, Did you find a good one?

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:44.320
Umm... If I'm taking a ground type and adapting it for space,

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.410
then maybe I should base it on the Zephyranthes.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.660
But, but i could also use the Thunderbolt version of the GM...

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.910
Please, take your time.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:00.300
Wow, you can build Gunpla here too.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:03.340
Not only building, you can also battle with them.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.720
How about it? Do you want to try?

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.680
But I've never built one before.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.220
It's alright. I'll teach you.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.560
Your Gunpla, let's see...

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.940
For a beginner, I'd recommend an SD Gundam.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:19.480
It's shorter, isn't it?

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:23.030
The original design is distorted to make it look cuter.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.400
Pick one that you like.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.490
What's Sekai doing, leaving Miss Hoshino behind?

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.240
Kamiki?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.790
Kousaka, why are you here?

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.500
I came to buy materials for my Gunpla.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.130
Why are you here, Kamiki?

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:41.750
What's with the sunglasses?

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:43.920
That's... Umm... Well... !

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.090
<b><i>Alright! I'll choose this Gunpla.</i></b>

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:46.680
That voice...

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:51.100
Actually, I feel kind of thirsty.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.640
Kousaka, let's get some tea.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.390
R-Really?

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:57.980
Of course! Come, let's go.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.310
Y-Yeah...

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.730
Nice recovery, big sis.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.860
What a wonderful surprise!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.740
Enjoy the rest of your date, Sekai.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.530
This is the one you ordered.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.450
A 1/100 scale Master Grade Queen Mantha.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.210
Wow, This is built really well.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:22.460
You're truly the great hope of the Shingyo school, Sakai.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:23.920
Thank you.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:27.880
But why order it from me, who lives in Osaka?

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:32.300
There are plenty of good builders in Tokyo, too.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:36.230
Actually, the pre-arranged person suddenly canceled on us.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:37.810
Who was it?

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.980
It was Kousaka Yuuma.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.360
Oh, so that's the story...

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.490
I'm his substitute, then?

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.150
Oh, no, that's not what I meant--

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.160
I'm feeling a little depressed now.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.280
I'm sorry, Sakai.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.500
Where did Sekai go?

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.790
Jigen Haoh style!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:12.300
Seiso-Geri!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:12.300
<i>Seiso-Geri: Holy Lance Kick</i>

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.220
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.310
How about that!? What do you think about my Gunpla!?

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.480
Sekai?

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.020
Ah, Hoshino!

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.440
I was a bit bored, so I played a battle.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.030
Where did this Gunpla come from?

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.360
I built it just now.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.950
You did, Sekai!?

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.950
Yup. The staff here taught me how to build it.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.080
What do you think of my Musha Godmaru?

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:39.080
Hey, Let's have another battle!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.250
It's my turn!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.460
Okay! I'll face you both together if you want.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.710
Who's that loser?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.010
What did you say?

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.260
Well, well, looks like people from Tokyo are shameless.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:55.640
They'll cancel an order, of fight against little kids.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.180
I give any match my all.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:15:59.600
That's my master's teaching.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.770
Don't boast if you can only build Gunpla like that.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:06.320
What did you say!?

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.690
Sorry, kids. Let me play against this guy first,

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.780
and I'll take revenge for you.

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:14.280
But you don't even have a Gunpla.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.910
I can build one of these right away.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.220
It's finished.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.270
A-Awesome.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.390
He built the Gunpla...

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.100
... in an instant.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:48.820
I'll teach you how people in Osaka play Gunpla Battle.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.650
<i>Gunpla Battle, combat mode, startup.</i>

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:55.320
<i>Model damage level, set to A.</i>

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.530
<i>Please set your GP base.</i>

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.450
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.130
<i>Field 3, Forest.</i>

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:12.880
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.720
Kamiki Sekai, Musha Godmaru, let's go!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.770
Here comes Kouki Gundam.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.150
Come one, Tokyo boy!

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:36.610
I'm not from Tokyo, but sure.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.580
Seiken-Zuki!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.580
<i>Seiken-Zuki: Holy Fist Thrust</i>

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.870
That's a weird technique, but...

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:47.540
He dodged it!?

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:48.420
He's fast!

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:52.340
Such techniques are ineffective with short SD arms and legs.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.930
As SD has its own fighting style!

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.090
It transformed!?

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.950
Ignoring the machine's traits, you're just pushing with force.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.740
How simple-minded!

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.620
Shine, beam crystal!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.380
What power.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:34.880
Sekai!

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:36.880
You loser.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:41.260
You're just forcing your own feelings on the Gunpla.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.680
The essence of Gunpla Battle is,

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.980
the Gunpla and the fighter battle together as one!

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:53.690
Unless you can use the   Jigen Haoh style in any situation,

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.610
you won't be able to win the championship.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:02.780
My Gunpla and I have to apply the Jigen Haoh style as one.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.120
If I were Musha Godmaru...

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.410
If I were Musha Godmaru itself...

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.090
If Musha Godmaru were myself...

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:31.980
Super mode?!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.020
So, it's the Explosive Form.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:38.240
With all my power in this fist...!

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.820
You have some guts.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:48.580
Kouki Gundam, super move!

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.170
How's that?

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:00.590
Not yet!

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:07.100
Take this...!

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.190
A flight form!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.240
Gunpla is freedom.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.990
Amid that limitless freedom. I materialized my thoughts.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:32.210
Yes, this is the model of my heart!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.710
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.420
Awesome!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.510
How was that? Wasn't I cool?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.840
Sekai...

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:46.300
My Gunpla... lost.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:47.930
I...

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.930
Now you get it.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.440
You're a big fish in a little pond.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:57.150
Just keep quiet, small fry.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:04.780
The essence of Gunpla Battle is, the Gunpla and the fighter battle together as one!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:07.160
Gunpla is freedom.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:13.410
Hoshino. I knew nothing about Gunpla Battle.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:18.500
But now I've realized a little bit what I'm missing.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:21.510
He taught me something, too.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:27.090
Gunpla lets me enchance my imagination and give it form.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:29.720
I'll practice hard!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:33.810
I'm definitely going to build it. My very own Gunpla.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:39.610
Wow, you two are so lovey-dovey.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.980
It's time to kiss now! Kiss!

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:45.150
Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:43.530
<b>What're you saying!?</b>

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:45.070
<b>We won't!</b>

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:48.070
Eh!? You're not going to kiss?

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.410
I said, we won't!

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.410
<b>I said, we won't!</b>

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.540
Thank you for the treat, Mirai.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:27.170
Oh, you're welcome.

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:29.800
That Gunpla...!

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:34.640
Awesome. So well build...

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:38.850
It's as good as my work, or no, even better.

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:42.350
This mark...!

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:44.860
It's him.

00:23:45.270 --> 00:23:46.610
You know this person?

00:23:46.780 --> 00:23:47.530
Yes.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.610
The guy who built this Gunpla is...   One of Osaka's top middle-school builders.

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:56.830
It's Minato Sakai of the Gunpla Shingyo school.

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:02.710
The qualifiers have finally begun.

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:05.540
We'll show you our Gunpla spirits!

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:07.800
Next Episode, "Dream and Challenge in Your Heart."

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:09.420
We are challengers!
